<p>The United States said on March 30 that it had resumed normal operations at its embassy in Caracas, restoring a full on-the-ground diplomatic presence in Venezuela after the post-2019 shutdown. The reopening follows the restoration of diplomatic ties after a January US military operation that removed Nicolás Maduro from power. The move marks a notable thaw between Washington and Caracas, ending years without direct US diplomatic activity inside Venezuela.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/WdknfZX3cVvboXPoA3v6V2u3ZG252NfsE8tMcVqBREfyBKBBnkm5qoVxBWPCCmiq-RBdqAty2h5tMpQetBt78XK_J7hy_t6S8tojylgByyWVXo_-20qD78NmGNW0N564DTopmwgeEqGWg-d3M1Js8G1V0qqOsYZuxoDi-JJusMzLAMoGWAGb58ys7jsFwKPPv9SBd3wuSN1613PhSBUY' alt='Image related to the reopening of the US embassy in Caracas after relations with Venezuela were restored.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Leadership transition: The Guardian reports that Delcy Rodríguez, who had been Maduro’s vice-president, is now serving as acting president as Washington restores embassy operations.</li><li>Trump-era break: PBS and SCMP note that the shutdown began during President Donald Trump’s first term, underscoring how long the diplomatic freeze lasted before the 2026 reset.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>US State Department: The department said the embassy in Caracas is back on a regular footing, restoring a normal US diplomatic presence inside the country. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/u-s-reopens-long-closed-embassy-in-venezuela-months-after-military-operation-to-remove-maduro'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>Trump administration: US officials cast the reopening as part of the post-Maduro reset in bilateral ties and a step toward a more stable relationship with Caracas. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/us-reopens-embassy-in-venezuela-after-seizing-nicolas-maduro/a-76599216'>Deutsche Welle</a>)</li><li>The Guardian: The paper tied the reopening to Washington’s work with the government of acting president Delcy Rodríguez, Maduro’s former vice-president. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/30/us-reopens-embassy-in-venezuela'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Euronews: In practical terms, US officials can again handle Venezuela-related diplomacy directly from Caracas instead of relying on a remote arrangement. (<a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/03/30/us-embassy-in-venezuela-formally-resumes-operations-after-seven-year-closure'>Euronews</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/u-s-reopens-long-closed-embassy-in-venezuela-months-after-military-operation-to-remove-maduro'>U.S. reopens long-closed embassy in Venezuela months after military operation to remove Maduro</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/us-reopens-embassy-in-venezuela-after-seizing-nicolas-maduro/a-76599216'>US reopens embassy in Venezuela after seizing Nicolas Maduro</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/americas/article/3348456/us-reopens-embassy-venezuela-months-after-military-operation-remove-maduro'>US reopens embassy in Venezuela months after military operation to remove Maduro</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/30/us-reopens-embassy-venezuela'>US reopens embassy in Venezuela in significant thawing of relations</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/03/30/us-embassy-in-venezuela-formally-resumes-operations-after-seven-year-closure'>US embassy in Venezuela formally resumes operations after seven-year closure</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/us-formally-reopens-caracas-embassy-as-ties-with-venezuela-warm'>US formally reopens Caracas embassy as ties with Venezuela warm</a> - straitstimes.com</li></ul>